WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:16.031
you're all here," Morb said, sneering.

2
00:00:16.051 --> 00:00:22.194
"You may have been able to trick those idiotic trolls, but you won't escape from me this time."

3
00:00:22.214 --> 00:00:24.576
"Run!" Perda yelled.

4
00:00:25.356 --> 00:00:26.477
"Not so fast."

5
00:00:26.977 --> 00:00:28.138
Morb waved his hand.

6
00:00:28.878 --> 00:00:31.940
A translucent green bubble appeared over the entire house.

7
00:00:32.672 --> 00:00:35.655
Perda skidded to a stop in front of the glowing green wall.

8
00:00:35.675 --> 00:00:37.957
"You can't do this!"

9
00:00:38.457 --> 00:00:38.897
she yelled.

10
00:00:39.718 --> 00:00:43.281
Rubbing both hands together, she aimed a Blast spell at the shield.

11
00:00:43.862 --> 00:00:46.604
The blast bounced off and shot back at her.

12
00:00:46.664 --> 00:00:48.986
She ducked, and it blew up a chair behind her.

13
00:00:49.706 --> 00:00:51.228
Morb threw back his head and laughed.

14
00:00:52.028 --> 00:00:53.850
"I should have used a shield sooner.

15
00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.492
That would have saved me a lot of trouble.

16
00:00:57.153 --> 00:01:00.816
But who could have guessed a few kids would be so hard to capture?

17
00:01:01.576 --> 00:01:03.638
In any case I've got you now."

18
00:01:04.759 --> 00:01:06.420
He turned and smirked at Zann.

19
00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.622
"Even you.

20
00:01:09.103 --> 00:01:11.425
Your grandfather is eager to see you.

21
00:01:12.246 --> 00:01:15.308
Perhaps you two can share a cell in my dungeon."

22
00:01:16.149 --> 00:01:17.270
Zann's heart pounded.

23
00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:18.331
"Now what?"

24
00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:19.092
he thought.

25
00:01:19.792 --> 00:01:21.414
They were truly trapped this time.

26
00:01:22.394 --> 00:01:24.216
Even Zing was shrinking away from Morb.

27
00:01:24.937 --> 00:01:28.420
As he looked around, desperate for ideas, Zann noticed something.

28
00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:33.041
That heavy wooden beam was still hanging in midair where his spell had frozen it.

29
00:01:34.141 --> 00:01:36.122
And Morb was just a few steps away!

30
00:01:36.902 --> 00:01:37.602
Zann gulped.

31
00:01:37.982 --> 00:01:43.684
Since early childhood he had been taught by his parents that one law in Magica was more important

32
00:01:43.724 --> 00:01:44.544
than any other.

33
00:01:45.264 --> 00:01:50.126
That law could be summed up in just a few simple words: Do no harm to others.

34
00:01:50.906 --> 00:01:53.207
But this was no time to worry about following the rules.

35
00:01:53.927 --> 00:01:57.808
He stepped sideways, so the beam now hung above the space between him and Morb.

36
00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:00.300
"Hey, Morb," he said.

37
00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:05.162
"I've got something to say to you—unless you're too scared to face a Red."

38
00:02:05.902 --> 00:02:08.983
Zann's friends looked startled, but Morb just chuckled.

39
00:02:09.003 --> 00:02:11.303
"Me, afraid of you?"

40
00:02:11.884 --> 00:02:13.484
Morb took a step toward Zann.

41
00:02:13.504 --> 00:02:19.926
"You obviously overestimate your own powers— just like your know-it-all grandfather."

42
00:02:20.726 --> 00:02:21.926
Morb took another step.

43
00:02:22.566 --> 00:02:24.587
The beam was now just above his head.

44
00:02:25.647 --> 00:02:27.808
If he looked up, he'd see it and move away.

45
00:02:28.616 --> 00:02:30.057
Zann had to act immediately.

46
00:02:30.077 --> 00:02:32.279
"Free," he whispered.

47
00:02:32.959 --> 00:02:35.921
The beam plummeted down and hit Morb square on the head.

48
00:02:36.642 --> 00:02:40.144
Morb grunted in surprise and crumpled to the ground, unconscious.

49
00:02:40.925 --> 00:02:43.686
As soon as Morb fell, the shield blinked out of sight.

50
00:02:43.707 --> 00:02:46.068
"Wow!" Perda cried.

51
00:02:46.088 --> 00:02:47.749
"That was great, Zann!"

52
00:02:47.769 --> 00:02:50.691
"Yeah. Let's get out of here!"

53
00:02:51.012 --> 00:02:51.592
Gliss added.

54
00:02:52.352 --> 00:02:54.774
Zing was already flying away from the ruined house.

55
00:02:55.495 --> 00:02:57.216
Darb, Perda, and Gliss followed.

56
00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:58.741
"Hurry, Zann!"

57
00:02:59.061 --> 00:02:59.621
Darb called.

58
00:02:59.641 --> 00:03:03.783
"Coming." Zann quickly reached under the table and grabbed the diary.

59
00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:07.165
Shoving it into his pocket, he raced after his friends.

60
00:03:08.246 --> 00:03:10.027
The group was soon back at the Hollow.

61
00:03:10.907 --> 00:03:13.328
"You don't think the beam killed Morb, do you?"

62
00:03:13.709 --> 00:03:14.289
Zann asked.

63
00:03:14.309 --> 00:03:16.810
"Definitely not," said Perda.

64
00:03:17.511 --> 00:03:19.592
"I saw him breathing when I ran past him."

65
00:03:19.612 --> 00:03:23.674
"But the way the shield just disappeared Zann began.

66
00:03:23.694 --> 00:03:27.536
"We learned about that in school," Gliss reminded him.

67
00:03:28.376 --> 00:03:32.119
"Certain types of spells require constant focus to maintain them.

68
00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:33.821
I guess it was one of those."

69
00:03:33.841 --> 00:03:36.383
"Don't worry, Zann," Darb said.

70
00:03:36.403 --> 00:03:40.947
"Even the do-no-harm-to-others rule makes an exception for emergencies."

71
00:03:41.807 --> 00:03:43.969
Zann flashed his friend a grateful smile.

72
00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:50.575
It was amazing how Darb could almost always guess what Zann was thinking, even without using any magic.

73
00:03:50.595 --> 00:03:52.656
"Okay," Zann said.

74
00:03:52.676 --> 00:03:56.660
"But that means Morb is going to be really angry when he wakes up.

75
00:03:57.416 --> 00:03:59.397
We'll have to be more careful than ever."

76
00:04:00.197 --> 00:04:01.117
Perda bit her lip.

77
00:04:01.417 --> 00:04:03.958
"He'll probably be watching for us at your house.

78
00:04:04.838 --> 00:04:07.079
How are we going to find that diary now?"

79
00:04:07.099 --> 00:04:10.520
"Oh!" Zann stuck his hand in his pocket.

80
00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:13.280
"I almost forgot—I found it."

81
00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:14.941
He pulled out the book.

82
00:04:15.401 --> 00:04:16.381
"That's the good news."

83
00:04:17.181 --> 00:04:18.422
"What's the bad news?"

84
00:04:18.842 --> 00:04:19.462
Perda asked.

85
00:04:20.202 --> 00:04:20.942
Zann grimaced.

86
00:04:20.962 --> 00:04:23.343
"It got damaged in the explosion."

87
00:04:24.103 --> 00:04:26.964
From the outside the diary appeared to be in pretty good shape.

88
00:04:27.948 --> 00:04:32.469
But as soon as Zann flipped it open, his friends could see that many of the interior pages

89
00:04:32.529 --> 00:04:35.090
were ripped, scorched, or missing altogether.

90
00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:37.371
"Wow," Perda said.

91
00:04:37.391 --> 00:04:41.292
"Do you think whatever Boz wanted the king and queen to see is still in there?"

92
00:04:41.312 --> 00:04:45.613
"Maybe I should read it and try to figure that out," Zann said.

93
00:04:46.613 --> 00:04:47.673
Gliss looked impatient.

94
00:04:47.693 --> 00:04:50.254
"We don't have time to sit around and read.

95
00:04:50.954 --> 00:04:53.215
We need to get that diary to the palace."

96
00:04:54.115 --> 00:04:55.676
"How are we supposed to do that?"

97
00:04:56.016 --> 00:04:56.636
Perda asked.

98
00:04:57.344 --> 00:04:59.706
"It would take days to reach First City on foot.

99
00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:02.128
And we can't use magic, remember?"

100
00:05:02.148 --> 00:05:08.412
"Plus traveling to the castle might not be worth the risk if the diary is damaged," Darb put

101
00:05:08.472 --> 00:05:09.973
in. "Zann's right.

102
00:05:10.273 --> 00:05:14.817
He should read it before we start a dangerous journey across Magica with Morb on our trail."

103
00:05:14.837 --> 00:05:20.360
"But we need to figure out what Morb is doing with my parents and all those other Reds,"

104
00:05:20.761 --> 00:05:21.441
Gliss argued.

105
00:05:21.461 --> 00:05:25.084
"It seems like nobody else has ever even heard of Morb.

106
00:05:25.824 --> 00:05:27.445
Jev didn't recognize his name."

107
00:05:28.506 --> 00:05:29.246
Zann shrugged.

108
00:05:29.266 --> 00:05:31.927
"That's because Jev is an idiot."

109
00:05:32.648 --> 00:05:36.190
He expected Gliss to protest since she seemed to like Jev.

110
00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:38.551
Instead she looked thoughtful.

111
00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:43.213
"We could try sending a spy fly to spy on Morb," she suggested.

112
00:05:43.233 --> 00:05:47.976
"That might tell us what he's doing, and give Zann time to read the diary."

113
00:05:47.996 --> 00:05:53.039
"But we can't send a spy fly without magic," Perda reminded her.

114
00:05:53.059 --> 00:05:57.781
"And we can't use magic, or Morb will know exactly where we are."

115
00:05:57.801 --> 00:06:01.083
"We can't use magic," Gliss said.

116
00:06:01.103 --> 00:06:03.705
"But someone else could use it for us.

117
00:06:04.245 --> 00:06:06.187
Someone who isn't being tracked by Morb.

118
00:06:06.927 --> 00:06:09.168
And I know the perfect person for the job."

119
00:06:09.188 --> 00:06:11.490
"Who?" Zann asked.

120
00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:12.991
Gliss smiled.

121
00:06:13.011 --> 00:06:14.271
"Jev, of course."
